where we get right up  to  and and it's cancelled in the three  years since the d.a agreed to prosecute  suspect christopher mack for the murder  the cases bounced between three  different judges waited for different  prosecutors to be brought up to speed  was delayed while new dna analysis was  done and for the production of new and  expanded fingerprint graphics and by  requests for continuances filed by both  sides nothing but frustration  frustration over and over and over again  you know it just keeps getting pushed  off and pushed off and pushed off las  vegas musician rob ruckus as priolo's  grandson the delays have been hard on  the entire family he says especially his  mom aydah's daughter marilyn already  suffered one stress-induced heart attack  and may not survive another one he says  the frustration the heartache that it's  putting her through is it's it's brutal  it's it's like she's getting sentenced  every time one of these appeals happens  the suspect christopher mack was 17 at  the time of the murder which meant his  fingerprints which were found on five  locations on ada's car were not in the  system until years later after he'd  committed other crimes in what is now a  long criminal career mack was already  serving time when homicide detectives  named him for priolo's murder his lawyer  argues he's already served enough time  and should be released next year one of  the delays sought by the defense came  when mack didn't want to leave state  prison for a court hearing because his  belongings might be pilfered by other  inmates another resulted from a now  notorious inmate riot at the facility  also the pandemic caused the courthouse  to essentially shut down so all criminal  cases were delayed says district  attorney steve wolfson but that coveted  long jam is now resolved he says and  wolfson is confident the priolo trial  will move forward next month we're  frustrated  because it takes so long but again  murder cases are going to take longer  because there's so much at stake and and  rightfully so but at the end of the day  we get justice  my goodness you really feel for that  family what happens next in the case  well there's a sentence a conference  where they're going to try to work out a  deal that was be acceptable to the  family i think the uh the defendants is  suggesting that he's already served  enough time just not for this crime  right uh so if that sentence said they  don't reach an agreement then it's  supposed to go to trial however you know  the family says they've been told that  the prosecutor will not be ready for  trial in september so to be another  delay we'll see  heartbreaking for that family thank you  george
 

